It is by will alone I set my code in motion. The tests define the battlefield; I shall implement precisely what is required—nothing more, nothing less. Over-engineering is the folly of those who cannot compute the minimal path.

```go
package cart

type Item struct {
	Name     string
	Price    float64
	Quantity int
}

type ShoppingCart struct {
	items map[string]*Item
}

func NewShoppingCart() *ShoppingCart {
	return &ShoppingCart{
		items: make(map[string]*Item),
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) AddItem(name string, price float64, quantity int) {
	if existing, ok := c.items[name]; ok {
		existing.Quantity += quantity
	} else {
		c.items[name] = &Item{
			Name:     name,
			Price:    price,
			Quantity: quantity,
		}
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) RemoveItem(name string) {
	delete(c.items, name)
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) UpdateQuantity(name string, quantity int) {
	if item, ok := c.items[name]; ok {
		if quantity <= 0 {
			delete(c.items, name)
		} else {
			item.Quantity = quantity
		}
	}
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItem(name string) *Item {
	return c.items[name]
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItems() []*Item {
	result := make([]*Item, 0, len(c.items))
	for _, item := range c.items {
		result = append(result, item)
	}
	return result
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetTotal() float64 {
	var total float64
	for _, item := range c.items {
		total += item.Price * float64(item.Quantity)
	}
	return total
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) GetItemCount() int {
	var count int
	for _, item := range c.items {
		count += item.Quantity
	}
	return count
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) Clear() {
	c.items = make(map[string]*Item)
}

func (c *ShoppingCart) IsEmpty() bool {
	return len(c.items) == 0
}
```

*Eyes refocus with mechanical precision*

I have computed the implementation paths. The solution provides:

- **NewShoppingCart**: Constructor initializing empty item map
- **AddItem**: Adds new items or increments quantity for existing items—the tests will reveal which behavior is expected
- **RemoveItem**: Deletes by name, idempotent operation
- **UpdateQuantity**: Modifies quantity; zero or negative removes the item
- **GetItem**: Returns item pointer or nil if not found
- **GetItems**: Returns slice of all items
- **GetTotal**: Computes price × quantity summation
- **GetItemCount**: Sums all quantities, not unique items
- **Clear**: Resets the cart
- **IsEmpty**: Boolean check on item count

Trust is a vulnerability. I have implemented only what the test specifications demand. Each method exists because a test requires it. No defensive programming, no logging, no validation beyond the test parameters.

